      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"the generator\",\"alternative_quotes\":[],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:97559638469f2f0643e9f550088b7bee3f5976c128f07de41c13b0412e540ff4\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:aee79caf6defa68093e64c982007b459521db3c877e73e6c218f934f9b5e5e0f\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:96a64cc35d8387e7e46add58630f863600ebb4d4d29797e6537785f526d3a4fa\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:13b7d9ae51381b3d9635cae789547141900d7969a0ec64951702f437714692d2\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:05f1e543c62163283848dea5c8f03f3c86e4103b5573d8e3123121837740d5e7\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:e90a5c6ad317cfbb6a074afaa8d013ec8cc499897d37cf42226f61f309bb43ef\"],\"choice_quote\":\"(1) If a container holding hazardous waste is not in good condition, or if it begins to leak, the generator must immediately transfer the hazardous waste from this container to a container that is in good condition and does not leak, or immediately transfer and manage the waste in a central accumulation area operated in compliance with § 262.16(b) or § 262.17(a).\",\"choice_text\":\"The generator must immediately transfer the hazardous waste to either: (1) a container that is in good condition and does not leak, or (2) a central accumulation area operated in compliance with § 262.16(b) or § 262.17(a).\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[\"(a) A generator may accumulate as much as 55 gallons of non-acute hazardous waste and/or either one quart of liquid acute hazardous waste listed in § 261.31 or § 261.33(e) of this chapter or 1 kg (2.2 lbs) of solid acute hazardous waste listed in § 261.31 or § 261.33(e) of this chapter in containers at or near any point of generation where wastes initially accumulate which is under the control of the operator of the process generating the waste, without a permit or interim status and without complying with the requirements of parts 124, 264 through 267, and 270 of this chapter, provided that all of the conditions for exemption in this section are met. A generator may comply with the conditions for exemption in this section instead of complying with the conditions for exemption in § 262.16(b) or § 262.17(a), except as required in § 262.15(a)(7) and (8). The conditions for exemption for satellite accumulation are:\"],\"defined_terms\":[],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":1614,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":1614,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Ae83b7297b741d59fb878775fd631eeb28a5aa35359e885bf29ca58f62f120732:1249:1614:sha256-819bb8cb1be80d00df9bdaa53929b892a7691e2f01bf10b41014a12c30c6c770\",\"quote\":\"(1) If a container holding hazardous waste is not in good condition, or if it begins to leak, the generator must immediately transfer the hazardous waste from this container to a container that is in good condition and does not leak, or immediately transfer and manage the waste in a central accumulation area operated in compliance with § 262.16(b) or § 262.17(a).\",\"start\":1249},{\"end\":1356,\"field\":\"actor\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Ae83b7297b741d59fb878775fd631eeb28a5aa35359e885bf29ca58f62f120732:1343:1356:sha256-f6b092ed2afc325805e09d578763e58caaaa697b8049773bb2a1e13b1a80ab28\",\"quote\":\"the generator\",\"start\":1343},{\"end\":1361,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Ae83b7297b741d59fb878775fd631eeb28a5aa35359e885bf29ca58f62f120732:1357:1361:sha256-4137b01e139589b7a1d3b3fc4da031d8ce5bb415808734e970c3a58ea0e98f0f\",\"quote\":\"must\",\"start\":1357},{\"end\":1614,\"field\":\"choice_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Ae83b7297b741d59fb878775fd631eeb28a5aa35359e885bf29ca58f62f120732:1249:1614:sha256-819bb8cb1be80d00df9bdaa53929b892a7691e2f01bf10b41014a12c30c6c770\",\"quote\":\"(1) If a container holding hazardous waste is not in good condition, or if it begins to leak, the generator must immediately transfer the hazardous waste from this container to a container that is in good condition and does not leak, or immediately transfer and manage the waste in a central accumulation area operated in compliance with § 262.16(b) or § 262.17(a).\",\"start\":1249},{\"end\":1614,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Ae83b7297b741d59fb878775fd631eeb28a5aa35359e885bf29ca58f62f120732:1249:1614:sha256-819bb8cb1be80d00df9bdaa53929b892a7691e2f01bf10b41014a12c30c6c770\",\"quote\":\"(1) If a container holding hazardous waste is not in good condition, or if it begins to leak, the generator must immediately transfer the hazardous waste from this container to a container that is in good condition and does not leak, or immediately transfer and manage the waste in a central accumulation area operated in compliance with § 262.16(b) or § 262.17(a).\",\"start\":1249},{\"end\":1247,\"field\":\"context:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Ae83b7297b741d59fb878775fd631eeb28a5aa35359e885bf29ca58f62f120732:322:1247:sha256-9d5462ca5acb5b64b79b4fb6c7300dcb44210d3f68fcb2c26e7ecdffde248bd6\",\"quote\":\"(a) A generator may accumulate as much as 55 gallons of non-acute hazardous waste and/or either one quart of liquid acute hazardous waste listed in § 261.31 or § 261.33(e) of this chapter or 1 kg (2.2 lbs) of solid acute hazardous waste listed in § 261.31 or § 261.33(e) of this chapter in containers at or near any point of generation where wastes initially accumulate which is under the control of the operator of the process generating the waste, without a permit or interim status and without complying with the requirements of parts 124, 264 through 267, and 270 of this chapter, provided that all of the conditions for exemption in this section are met. A generator may comply with the conditions for exemption in this section instead of complying with the conditions for exemption in § 262.16(b) or § 262.17(a), except as required in § 262.15(a)(7) and (8). The conditions for exemption for satellite accumulation are:\",\"start\":322}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:20424c21416a436ed63ce4a0193da6c95b06dc9679d2a35776995095fe846360\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"requirement\",\"logic_text\":\"\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:e90a5c6ad317cfbb6a074afaa8d013ec8cc499897d37cf42226f61f309bb43ef\",\"modality\":\"must\",\"modality_quote\":\"must\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:01f54f9e1f6719e71642c8ced97d26ddbc3da95488b488a8d85b27b1c5dada79\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(1) If a container holding hazardous waste is not in good condition, or if it begins to leak, the generator must immediately transfer the hazardous waste from this container to a container that is in good condition and does not leak, or immediately transfer and manage the waste in a central accumulation area operated in compliance with § 262.16(b) or § 262.17(a).\",\"references\":[\"§ 262.16(b)\",\"§ 262.17(a)\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:183fc3e0a219b0823f0a3d6e7fda1272c2b7e883d683c10b38fe154be76fc9ac\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(1) If a container holding hazardous waste is not in good condition, or if it begins to leak, the generator must immediately transfer the hazardous waste from this container to a container that is in good condition and does not leak, or immediately transfer and manage the waste in a central accumulation area operated in compliance with § 262.16(b) or § 262.17(a).\"],\"scope_text\":\"If a container holding hazardous waste is not in good condition, or if it begins to leak\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":1249,\"summary\":\"Under the conditions for exemption for satellite accumulation, if a container holding hazardous waste is not in good condition, or if it begins to leak, the generator must immediately transfer the hazardous waste from this container to a container that is in good condition and does not leak, or immediately transfer and manage the waste in a central accumulation area operated in compliance with § 262.16(b) or § 262.17(a).\",\"target_ids\":[],\"term_refs\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
